# iOS Complexity & Maintainability

Guidelines (not absolute). Exceptions OK for SwiftUI `body`, generated code, tests, mocks — document when intentional.

## Targets (refactor above warning)

| Metric | Target | Warning | Hard limit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Function length | ≤ 30 lines | > 30 | > 50 |
| Cyclomatic complexity | ≤ 8 | 9–12 | > 12 |
| Cognitive complexity | ≤ 15 | — | — |
| Parameters | ≤ 4 | 5–6 | ≥ 7 → value object |
| Nesting depth | ≤ 2 | 3 | ≥ 4 |
| Local variables | ≤ 8 | > 8 | > 10 |
| Returns per function | ≤ 3 | > 3 | — |
| File length | ≤ 300 | > 400 | > 600 |
| Type length | ≤ 300 | > 400 | — |
| Functions per type | ≤ 20 | > 25 | — |
| Stored properties | ≤ 15 | > 20 | — |
| Injected dependencies | 3–6 | 7–8 | ≥ 9 → split type |

## Do

- One responsibility per function/type; descriptive names (`fetchUserProfile`, not `doTask`)
- Early `guard` / flat code — no nested `if { if { if {`
- Prefer DI + protocols over singletons; business logic in ViewModel / UseCase / Repository — never in SwiftUI `body`
- Default to `private`; keep public API minimal
- Comments explain **why**, not **what**
- Rule of Three for duplication (extract on the third copy — don’t abstract early)
- Composition over inheritance; readability over cleverness

## Don’t

```swift
// ❌ Deep nesting
if loggedIn {
    if order.isValid {
        if payment.isAvailable { ... }
    }
}

// ❌ God type / too many collaborators
class OrderManager { /* networking + DB + analytics + auth */ }

// ❌ Parameter laundry list — use a request/value type instead
createOrder(user, address, coupon, payment, note, deliveryTime)
```

```swift
// ✅ Flat + focused
guard user.isLoggedIn else { return }
guard order.isValid else { return }
process(order)
```

## When over limit

Extract helpers, split into Repository / Service / ViewModel / Coordinator, replace large `switch` with strategy/polymorphism, group params into a struct.

## Aligns with

`iOSApp/AGENT.md` style (§11–13) and existing `AppContainer` DI — no third-party DI library required.
